# RTK — Rust Token Killer (wajib)

Use **RTK** for shell commands in this project. Cursor Shell tool calls are rewritten globally via `rtk hook cursor` in `~/.cursor/hooks.json`.

## Shell commands (automatic)

Normal shell invocations are rewritten transparently (`git status` → `rtk git status`). Prefer shell + RTK over dumping huge raw output into context.

## When hooks do not apply

Built-in read/search tools may bypass the hook. Prefer these RTK equivalents when output would be large:

```bash
rtk read path/to/file.go
rtk read path/to/file.svelte -l aggressive
rtk grep "pattern" apps/
rtk find apps/frontend -name "*.svelte"
rtk git status
rtk git diff
rtk git log -5
```

## CubyCloud commands (via RTK)

```bash
cd apps/frontend && rtk bun run check
cd apps/frontend && rtk bun run build
cd apps/backend && rtk go test ./...
cd apps/backend && rtk go build ./cmd/server
```

## Meta

```bash
rtk gain              # savings analytics
rtk proxy <cmd>       # raw output when debugging filter issues
```

Install (once per machine): `brew install rtk` then `rtk init -g --agent cursor --auto-patch`.

See `RTK.md` at repo root for full reference.
